{
  "version": 8,
  "dashboardId": "business_metrics",
  "title": "Business Metrics",
  "description": "Business signal only: registrations, users by auth type, orders and their delivery state, and email outcomes. HTTP status codes are deliberately NOT here — they are technical health, not business, and each service's own Golden Signals dashboard already carries them. Two tabs: \"At a glance\" for the current number of each metric, \"Trends\" for how it moved. PANELS USE PromQL, NOT SQL: the UI dispatches on queryType, and a metrics stream queried with queryType sql renders 'Error Loading Data' without ever issuing a search request. Dimension names arrive prefixed and lowercased (CloudWatch `Service` -> `dimensions_service`), and the metric name becomes the stream name (amazonaws.com/3MRAI/orders_total -> amazonaws_com_3mrai_orders_total). Gauges use max(); counters use sum().",
  "role": "",
  "owner": "3MRAI",
  "created": "2026-08-12T00:00:00.000Z",
  "tabs": [
    {
      "tabId": "trends",
      "name": "Trends",
      "panels": [
        {
          "id": "users_registered",
          "type": "bar",
          "title": "Users registered",
          "description": "Registrations per 5-minute interval. A counter bucketed with sum_over_time so each bar is \"how many in this interval\" — the raw series carries one entry per collector start_time (779 of them over 2h), which is why it must be aggregated. max by(), not sum by(): those duplicate series would otherwise be added together and report a multiple of the truth. Empty intervals read 0 because the counter is seeded at 0 on a fixed clock.",
          "config": {
            "show_legends": false,
            "decimals": 0
          },
          "queryType": "promql",
          "queries": [
            {
              "query": "max by (dimensions_service) (sum_over_time(amazonaws_com_3mrai_users_registered_total[5m]))",
              "customQuery": true,
              "fields": {
                "stream": "amazonaws_com_3mrai_users_registered_total",
                "stream_type": "metrics",
                "x": [],
                "y": [],
                "z": [],
                "filter": {
                  "filterType": "group",
                  "logicalOperator": "AND",
                  "conditions": []
                },
                "breakdown": []
              },
              "config": {
                "promql_legend": "registrations",
                "layer_type": "scatter",
                "weight_fixed": 1
              }
            }
          ],
          "layout": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 96,
            "h": 15,
            "i": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "users_by_auth_type",
          "type": "pie",
          "title": "Users by sign-in method",
          "description": "Current split of live users by HOW they sign in — a composition, so a pie: the two slices are parts of one whole. Not 'has a password': a passwordless account does have a Cognito password (signUp requires one), it is simply never given to the user and password login is rejected for them. The ALL series is excluded — it is the pre-summed total and would swallow the whole circle.",
          "config": {
            "show_legends": true,
            "decimals": 0
          },
          "queryType": "promql",
          "queries": [
            {
              "query": "label_replace(label_replace(max by (dimensions_haspassword) (amazonaws_com_3mrai_users_total{dimensions_haspassword!=\"ALL\"}), \"method\", \"Password login\", \"dimensions_haspassword\", \"true\"), \"method\", \"Email OTP\", \"dimensions_haspassword\", \"false\")",
              "customQuery": true,
              "fields": {
                "stream": "amazonaws_com_3mrai_users_total",
                "stream_type": "metrics",
                "x": [],
                "y": [],
                "z": [],
                "filter": {
                  "filterType": "group",
                  "logicalOperator": "AND",
                  "conditions": []
                },
                "breakdown": []
              },
              "config": {
                "promql_legend": "{method}",
                "layer_type": "scatter",
                "weight_fixed": 1
              }
            }
          ],
          "layout": {
            "x": 96,
            "y": 0,
            "w": 96,
            "h": 15,
            "i": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "orders_total",
          "type": "line",
          "title": "Orders — total (Orders service)",
          "description": "The true live order count, from Orders' own table. Compare with the next panel: orders_total minus (DELIVERED + IN_PROGRESS) is the number of orders whose init-tracking call failed — a failure mode TrackingInitResult.cs documents as deliberately accepted. Normally zero.",
          "config": {
            "show_legends": false,
            "decimals": 0
          },
          "queryType": "promql",
          "queries": [
            {
              "query": "max(amazonaws_com_3mrai_orders_total)",
